==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{He.}} {{term|הבל||tr=hevel|sc=HEchar|breath, vapor; vanity}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeɪbəl/}}

====Homophones====
* [[able]]

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{biblical character}} The son of [[Adam]] and [[Eve]] who was killed by his brother [[Cain]].
# {{given name|male|from Hebrew|}}.

====Quotations====
* '''1611''' — [[w:King James Version of the Bible|King James Version of the Bible]], ''[[s:Bible (King James)/Genesis|Genesis]] 4:8''
*: And Cain talked with '''Abel''' his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against '''Abel''' his brother, and slew him.

